From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000029
Subject: [PATCH] Shells pay their skill costs

The immortality guard in status_damage() refused everything positive for a shell without the
mortal flag, including the SP a skill costs: skill_consume_requirement() charges it with
status_zap(), which is status_damage() with no source. Immortal shells cast for nothing.

An immortal shell now refuses only what someone else does to it. With no source, SP and AP go
through (skill costs, and the upkeep status_charge() takes for maintained statuses), and HP is
dropped, since poison and bleeding ticks have no source either. Mortal shells are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/map/status.cpp b/src/map/status.cpp
index eabbed2..618eefa 100644
--- a/src/map/status.cpp
+++ b/src/map/status.cpp
@@ -1501,12 +1501,18 @@ int32 status_damage(block_list *src,block_list *target,int64 dhp, int64 dsp, int
 	nullpo_ret(target);
 
 	// Population shells are immortal by default; only shells with PSF::Mortal (Flags: mortal) take damage.
+	// An immortal shell still pays its own way: SP and AP with no source are what skills and
+	// maintained statuses cost (status_zap, status_charge), so those go through. HP never does,
+	// since poison and bleeding have no source either.
 	if (target->type == BL_PC) {
 		map_session_data *pop_sd = BL_CAST(BL_PC, target);
 		if (pop_sd != nullptr && population_engine_is_population_pc(pop_sd->id)
-		    && !population_engine_shell_is_mortal(pop_sd)
-		    && (hp > 0 || sp > 0 || ap > 0))
-			return 0;
+		    && !population_engine_shell_is_mortal(pop_sd)) {
+			if (src != nullptr && (hp > 0 || sp > 0 || ap > 0))
+				return 0;
+			if (hp > 0)
+				hp = 0;
+		}
 	}
 
 	if(sp && !(target->type&BL_CONSUME))
